{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779504094,"nonce":"Z0gWZSuWgJ334HGECxS4kuGO6uk=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ0Bjg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/163","origin":"github"},"title":"AML SVS probe outputting all-NUL bytes on /dev/ttyS0 (in-water + dry)","message":"## Symptom\n\nDuring [#160](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/160) (2026-05-22 deployment), the AML SVS probe was **silent on `/dev/ttyS0` in-water** — serial line producing **all-NUL bytes** (0x00) rather than parseable Valeport-format sentences. Same symptom as the dry pre-launch state (gabby log §4c), persisting under water.\n\nChain:\n- AML probe (physical) → gabby `/dev/ttyS0` → gabby `sound_speed_bridge` → ROS topic `/bizzy/sensors/sound_speed/sound_speed` + UDP to `mercat:20003` (Valeport format for M3)\n\nThe bridge parses what it sees on the serial port; all-NUL bytes parse to NaN. ROS topic publishes NaN; M3 doesn't get usable sound-speed updates.\n\n## Likely causes (not yet diagnosed)\n\nThis is **hardware/config side**, not parser. Probe is not generating output. Candidates:\n\n1. **Probe configuration** — power-on state may have left the probe in a non-streaming mode (e.g., command-mode rather than auto-output, wrong baud rate, sleep state).\n2. **Power supply** — probe needs a specific voltage; check the cable + power injection setup.\n3. **Wiring** — TX/RX swap, ground reference, RS-232 vs. RS-485 level mismatch.\n4. **Hardware fault** — probe failure (last working: prior deployments).\n\n## Class-prep impact\n\n**Required for June 2026 Summer Hydro class**: M3 sonar needs sound-speed updates for correct depth measurement. Without AML output, M3 falls back to manufacturer-default sound speed (~1500 m/s) and depth measurements drift in fresh water (Lake Massabesic has substantially lower sound speed than sea water).\n\nPre-class action: bench-test the probe, verify config (auto-streaming mode, correct baud), inspect wiring. If probe is faulty, contact AML / arrange replacement.\n\nA separate stand-in path exists on mercat ([`aml_bridge.ps1`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/tree/jazzy/bizzyboat_project11/mercat) running AML COM3 → UDP to M3:20003) but it has its own quirks (CRCRLF terminator breaking M3's custom-sensor parser) and isn't a long-term replacement for the gabby pipeline.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter fix:\n- `cat /dev/ttyS0` on gabby shows recognizable Valeport-format ASCII sentences.\n- `/bizzy/sensors/sound_speed/sound_speed` publishes valid (non-NaN) values.\n- M3 receives updates on UDP:20003 (check via Wireshark / M3 console).\n\n## Context\n\n- Originating deployment: #160 (2026-05-22)\n- Gabby log: `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_gabby_logs.md` §4c (dry) + §5a (in-water, all-NUL bytes)\n- Hard deadline: dev freeze 2026-06-04\n\nPart of #160.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}